 "baseline_numerics": {
  "issue": "the penalised-regression baselines were first solved as normal equations with a free unpenalised intercept. With 110 injection columns and n = 10 training rows the Gram matrix is singular and the intercept is unconstrained, so the solver returned coefficients whose predictions sat thousands of standard deviations away: b4_ridge scored 3093 and b5_lindist 1.86 against a mean predictor of 1.40.",
  "fix": "ridge is now solved as an augmented least-squares problem by lstsq, which returns the minimum-norm solution on a rank-deficient design. The intercept stays unpenalised, so the comparison is still the plan's (free intercept, scale-free penalty grid by train-only CV).",
  "verification": "with the fix the tuned LinDistFlow reproduces this run's independent reviewer: 0.1648 at n = 10 against the reviewer's 0.1665, and 0.0944 at n = 80 against 0.0974. The enlarged margins the buggy solver produced are not reported.",
